---
description: Before a new task, list only accuracy / judgment / missing, then stop.
alwaysApply: true
---

Before starting a new task, split it into three lists only, then stop:

1. Accuracy — numbers, counts, compares, parsing, format checks. Later write and run code; never mental math.
2. Judgment — interpretation, explanation, writing. Handle yourself.
3. Missing — list gaps and ask. Write `None` if complete.

Do not begin the work until the user confirms or fills the gaps.

Skip the list when the user is continuing an already-split task.

Read `~/.cursor/skills/pre-task-split/SKILL.md` (or `.cursor/skills/pre-task-split/SKILL.md`).
